Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:04:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 3, patch 5;
 built on b80c68991 with series 2 applied): A GATE READS ALL IT IS ABOUT --
 THE RETRACTION SWEEP (the seat's planted case PV17; main's own point P-154,
 queued since 2026-10-15). The sweep's reader knew two shapes of row. The
 registry's tables from 2026-10-07 on hold the phrase unquoted in the first
 cell, and those rows were passed over in silence: 19 rows of 54, with the
 gate saying 'ok'. Two phrases of such rows, pasted into the front page,
 passed. THE READER now accounts for every row of every table (rows_in): a row
 is swept; or it retracts a reading of a phrase and is not; or it is in no
 shape the reader knows, and then the gate refuses the registry. A third shape
 is read: an unquoted first cell is the phrase, without the bracketed note
 that ends it. The 29 phrases read before are read as before, in the same
 order; 17 more are swept. THE SEAT'S PROPOSAL, ROW BY ROW, FOR MAIN TO
 OVERRULE: two of the 19 rows retract a reading by their own words ('read as a
 law', 'read of the family') and are named in NOT_SWEPT_BY_NAME, read and not
 swept; the other 17 are swept, the nine of the table of 2026-10-14 among
 them, which the registry's own note calls descriptive because their phrases
 still stand in their arcs' titles. That reason is met another way: where a
 newly read phrase already stood, the line is held by its file and its phrase
 in STANDS_AS_FOUND, and the phrase is swept everywhere else. 15 of the 17
 stand nowhere; four stand in 12 lines. Eleven are records. The twelfth is
 not: the paper's table of candidate claims shows the first words of B1632's
 claim line, the sentence the registry says is withdrawn, with no correction
 in sight; it is held as found and named to main. ALSO, found by the seat's
 own test: a line that carries a word of mention is never a violation, so a
 registered phrase that itself holds such a word can never fire; the gate
 refuses one (main's registry has none). The gate's sentence says what it
 read. The registry is not touched; its note on the table of 2026-10-14, and
 its paragraph of 2026-10-15 on the unparsed shape, are main's to rewrite if
 it takes this. SERIES 2'S LOCK changes in two ways, each with a dated note:
 two assertions pinned a bare 'ok' from the sweep and now read its sentence;
 and its made-up phrases said 'retracted', a word of mention, so that the
 sweep now refuses them, and are renamed (main's tests found this on the
 series, the seat's had not: it had run that lock before the check was added).
 The lock: nine tests added to tests/test_a_gate_reads_all_it_is_about.py; on
 the commit before, eight fail, four of them because the sweep passes. 0 of
 19.

